    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500-a1">

                <pb facs="0811" n="715" xml:id="pg715"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure “1” in No. 44.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>Juan Bautista Garcia, encharged with the Presidency of the United States of
                    Venezuela:</p>
                <p>The forces of the government having recovered Giudad Bolivar and freed the state
                    of Guayaria from enemies, it is therefore decreed: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. That the waters of the
                            Orinoco in all their extensions, embracing all its mouths as far as
                            Ciudad Bolivar, he opened to general commerce, and the blockade on the
                            coast of the same river suspended; and in consequence, the decree of
                            October 2, 1871, that established such blockade is abrogated.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 2. The minister of war and
                            marine will be charged with the execution of this decree and of
                            communicating it to whom it may concern.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Given in <placeName>Caracas</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-04">4th of May, 1872, ninth of the
                            law and fourteenth of the federation</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JUAN B. GARCIA. <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of War and
                                    Marine</hi>.</item>
                            <item>JUAN T. PEREZ,</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
